The upstream README requires CUDA 12.x for training and recommends an H200.
Evaluation falls back to CPU eager float32 (their evaluators/common.py).
Fused Triton kernels are CUDA-only; on CPU the repo's dense reference
attention is used. This app does not vendor upstream source. run_all.sh
clones the pinned commit into work/ebr (gitignored).

No paper figures are copied. Full-test numbers quoted from the paper
(99.4% / 99.9% on Sudoku-Extreme, 345× FLOPs) were not re-run.

